'''C-21 Highsinger''' was a [[Battle droid|combat droid]] [[bounty hunter]] that operated during the [[Clone Wars]]. He was part of [[Krayt's Claw]], a syndicate of bounty hunters that included [[Boba Fett]], [[Latts Razzi]], [[Dengar]], [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]], and [[Oked]]. He had extensive modifications, including precision-engineered [[servomotor]]s and manipulators. Although a deadly combat droid, C-21 Highsinger had his battle programming pushed beyond its limits when defending [[Otua Blank]]'s [[subtram]] from the swift [[Kage Warriors]]. Later in the Clone War, Highsinger was with the other members of Krayt's Claw,  worked when Boba Fett guided former [[Jedi Master]] [[Quinlan Vos]] to find former [[Sith apprentice]] [[Asajj Ventress]] and enlist her support in a mission to assassinate her former master, [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] leader [[Count]] [[Dooku]].

Highsinger continued to work with Razzi into the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. After they engaged and captured [[Unidentified four-armed alien|the alien]], Ventress and [[Lyco Strata]] appeared. The four of them worked together to acquire an [[Imperial shield relay unit]] from an [[Unidentified Imperial crawler|Imperial crawler]].

==Biography==
===Hunting Jango Fett===
C-21 Highsinger was a [[droid]] [[bounty hunter]] active in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="JF 4" /> Around [[33 BBY]],<ref name="Jango Date">{{JangoFettSeriesDate}}</ref> Highsinger joined the hunt for fellow [[bounty]] [[hunter]]s [[Jango Fett]] and [[Aurra Sing]]. In the end, Fett [[Skirmish on Jaloria|defeated their pursuers]] with a [[missile]] from his [[jetpack]], with the blast severing Highsinger's arm. Highsinger claimed his severed limb and sat amidst the flames.<ref name="JF 4" />

===The Clone Wars===
====Safe cargo objective====
During the [[Clone Wars]], Highsinger joined [[Krayt's Claw]], the group of [[bounty hunter]]s put together by<ref name="Bounty" /> Jango's son<ref name="Join the Battle" /> [[Boba Fett]] in order to undertake a mission on the [[planet]] of [[Quarzite]]. The hunters were joined by [[Asajj Ventress]]&mdash;although they were unaware of her identity&mdash;after she [[Death|killed]] one of the [[Oked|members]] of their team. The group was tasked with [[Safe cargo objective|guarding]] a large wooden chest aboard a [[subtram]], which was to be delivered to the [[Belugan]] [[Otua Blank]]. As the hunters spread out in anticipation of a confrontation, Highsinger was stationed near the cargo. Though the trip began easily enough, soon the tram was beset by [[Kage Warriors]], who sought the cargo for themselves.<ref name="Bounty" />

[[File:TurboliftTransportArea-Bounty.png|thumb|left|275px|Highsinger and the crew on Quarzite]]
One by one, the hunters fell. Though Highsinger was one of the last hunters standing, the Kage Warriors' leader, [[Krismo Sodi]], was able to dispatch the [[droid]] by linking him with fellow hunter [[Latts Razzi]] as she was thrown from the train. Highsinger fell beside Razzi, though both survived. In his absence, Fett too was bested by Sodi, who soon revealed that the cargo was his sister, [[Pluma Sodi]], who was to be forcibly [[Marriage|wed]] to Blank. Ventress, having suffered many changes in her recent past, ended up placing Fett within the chest and delivering him to Blank, collecting both a [[bounty]] from the [[warlord]] as well as from the [[Kage]] Warriors for freeing Pluma. She then shared the first bounty with Highsinger and the others, telling them that Fett would join them soon enough before departing.<ref name="Bounty" />

====Mission to Serenno====
In the second [[Standard year|year]] of the Clone Wars, Highsinger and several other members of Krayt's Claw including Fett, Razzi, and [[Embo]] were frequenting a [[Unidentified bar (Level 1313)|bar]] in [[Coruscant]]'s [[Level 1313]] when they were visited by the undercover [[Jedi Master]] [[Quinlan Vos]]. Vos had been dispatched by the [[Jedi High Council]] on a mission to assassinate the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] leader [[Count]] [[Dooku]] and had been partnered up with Asajj Ventress, a [[Dathomirian]] [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] who had once been Dooku's [[Sith apprentice]]. Fett informed Vos that Ventress was hunting a [[Volpai]] fugitive named [[Moregi]] on [[Pantora]]. Vos [[Capture of Moregi|traveled]] to Pantora where he managed to partner up as a bounty hunter before revealing his true identity and enlisting Ventress' support to [[Death|kill]] Dooku.<ref name="Dark Disciple" />

Following the failure of Vos and Ventress' [[Mission to Raxus Secundus|assassination attempt]], Ventress came to enlist the aid of Krayt's Claw. Fett was visited by her at [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] on [[Tatooine]] by Ventress, who wanted to rescue her partner and lover from Dooku, offering them a significant sum of credits to help her. They agreed, and Highsinger and the other Krayt's Claw members traveled on Fett's [[starship]] ''[[Slave I]]'' to [[Serenno]] on a [[Mission to Serenno (Krayt's Claw)|mission]] to infiltrate [[Castle Serenno]] and rescue Vetnress' partner. While Ventress infiltrated Dooku's palace, Highsinger and his associates staged a diversion and attack several [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] vehicles and droids. They even managed to snare Dooku under some webbing but were forced to flee when Vos spurned Ventress' rescue and openly sided with Dooku.<ref name="Dark Disciple" />

===Imperial Era===
[[File:RazziHighsingerVentressTogetherAgain-TotUFriends.png|thumb|300px|Highsinger and Razzi continued working together during the Imperial Era.]]
During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], Highsinger continued to work with Razzi. The two collaborated to hunt down a target who was wanted dead-or-alive. As they engaged [[Unidentified four-armed alien|the individual]], the familiar face of Ventress appeared, alongside a young boy, who identified himself as [[Lyco Strata|Lyco]]. After Highsinger shot the target and killed them, Highsinger dragged them towards [[Latts Razzi's ship|their ship]] as Razzi and Ventress spoke about intel the latter was hoping to receive.<ref name="Friends">{{TOTU|Friends}}</ref>

Highsinger, Razzi, Ventress and Strata traveled to the [[Cassaro shipyard]] on [[Cassaro]], in hopes of acquiring an [[Imperial shield relay unit]] that would direct Strata towards [[Quinlan Vos]] and [[Hidden Path|the Path]]. Highsinger, Strata and Ventress [[Heist at Cassaro shipyard|infiltrated]] an [[Unidentified Imperial crawler|Imperial crawler]] that was transporting [[ISD-72x shield generator dome|shield generators]] to [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial I''-class Star Destroyers]]. During the mission, Highsinger was discovered by an [[Imperial officer]] discovered Highsinger hiding under [[Crawler 187]] who shot him, prompting several [[stormtrooper]]s to attack Highsinger and Ventress. During the ensuing battle, Strata lost the shield relay unit, which led to Razzi ordering Highsinger to capture Strata instead, as he was worth twice the price of the relay unit. However, Ventress soon entered Razzi's ship through a hatch, cutting Highsinger across his torso with [[Asajj Ventress's lightsaber|her lightsaber]], while Strata restrained him with [[Lyco Strata's lightsaber|his own lightsaber]]. Ventress then forced Razzi to take them into [[hyperspace]]. After they entered hyperspace, Razzi was forced to give Ventress and Strata the coordinates to the Path.<ref name="Friends" />

During the [[Galactic Civil War]], Highsinger was among the bounty hunters hired by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] to return [[Doctor]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra|Aphra]] to him, after she was [[Battle of Vrogas Vas|captured]] by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] on [[Vrogas Vas]].<ref name="Darth Vader 16">[[Darth Vader (2015) 16|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 16]]</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Highsinger was a heavily modified [[Battle droid|combat droid]] of uncertain origin,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Gender|masculine programming]]<ref name="Bounty" /> who stood at 2.25 [[meter]]s (7 [[Foot|feet]], 5 inches) tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and had [[Color|red]] [[sensor]]s.<ref name="Bounty" /> Highsinger valued his independence, but agreed to work with Krayt's Claw on several occasions,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> as he provided firepower for the group on Quarzite and Serenno.<ref name="Bounty" /><ref name="Dark Disciple" />

As Highsinger was unable to speak [[Galactic Basic Standard]], he was not a frequent conversationalist, and often only spoke when addressed directly. When Highsinger did speak,<ref name="Bounty" /> the droid spoke an unknown droid dialect.<ref name="Light and Dark">{{StoryCite|story=The Lost Nightsister|book=The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark}}</ref> He was a straightforward operator, focusing on the job at hand. His torso was rotatable at the pelvic mount, which allowed him to perform rapid blaster attacks to eliminate multiple opponents within a circular area around him. Combined with his advanced servomotors, this made Highsinger a formidable combatant in close-quarters, even able to hold his own against skilled [[Species|organic]] [[humanoid]]s like the Kage Warriors.<ref name="Bounty" />

==Skills and abilities==
Highsinger's superhuman reflexes, speed and agility enabled him to be a terrifyingly efficient combat machine, excelling at armed and [[unarmed combat]], as well as martial arts.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> While Highsinger rotated and fired with his rapid speed, everyone, including allies such as Boba Fett had to remain out of harm's way. Highsinger's reflexes and speed combination proved lethal as he opened fire on the Kage Warriors.<ref name="Bounty" /> Highsinger was also an expert tracker.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Equipment==
Highsinger had a [[wrist blaster]] built into his arm. He also had a [[X-8 Night Sniper]] and an [[E-5C heavy blaster rifle]].<ref name="Bounty" /> In an earlier mission, Highsinger used an [[E-5 blaster rifle]].<ref name="JF 4" />

==Behind the scenes==
Before the cancellation of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series, Highsinger was set to make an appearance during a four-episode arc starring Boba Fett and [[Cad Bane]]. In a clip revealed during the Animated Origins and Unexpected Fates panel at [[Celebration Orlando]] in 2017, Highsinger was seen siding with Cad Bane during a stand-off against Boba Fett and other bounty hunters, restraining two hostages.<ref name="CO 17 AOaUF panel">{{SWYouTube|85Jw-63YNYI|Star Wars Celebration Orlando 2017: Animated Origins and Unexpected Fates}}</ref>

